{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines","id":557071,"title":"Bloodlines.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-16T11:12:04-07:00","id":557071,"title":"Bloodlines.","content":"Hi everyone =D<br /> <br /> Potentially another scrub question here. I'm trying to wrap my mind around bloodlines. 1E, 2E, doesn't matter. I understand the concept, a bunch of like-minded individuals, generally from the same clan, group up and form there own faction/clan. Okay, cool. Makes sense. The part that I'm having issues with is having others join that bloodline. From what I've read, you need to be of x-clan, and you need to consume vitae from someone of that Bloodline (or was it the founding member? Can't recall) So for Brujah (Bruja), one needs to be a Gangrel and drink the vitae of a Brujah. Why? Can not anyone who embraces the anarchist/bike gang lifestyle in theory be a Brujah? <br /> <br /> Or for example, the one that I keep thinking about is old school Malkavian. (I prefer them to Malkovian and refuse to acknowledge them, I will however, accept that they are a bloodline). I can imagine that a Malkavian's vitae can cause the drinker to be at risk for developing the 'Madness'. Why would one need to be Ventrue in order for this to happen? (yes yes, can house rule things in, but in general <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> TL;DR why are Bloodlines restricted to certain clans. Ex. Gangrel -&gt; Brujah?<br /> <br /> Thanks =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:23:06-07:00","id":557109,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines aren't just groups of like-minded individuals of the same Clan. They're actually offshoots of the parent Clan, which is why they're called Bloodlines. So just like you need to drink some of your Sire's Vitae to become a vampire, you need to drink the vitae of a member of the Bloodline in order to become one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:27:27-07:00","id":557116,"title":"","content":"I am only familiar with 2e. I say this because 2e is fairly skimpy on the information on Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> That said, here is my understanding:<br /> A sufficiently powerful vampire may have their blood changed by... whatever. It isn't a matter of factions or ideals, it's a matter of the founder internalizing and manifesting what amounts to a mutation of the Blood. The non-2e fluff I've read suggests this is usually not a conscious decision, though it could be. So it's more like the vampire's actions and ideals direct the mutation.<br /> <br /> As such, drinking the blood of a member of the bloodline is similar to uplifting a Revenant. It's changing the blood of the vampire, not just joining a faction. This is also why it's easier to join the bloodline of someone closer in relation to you. You can join your Sire's bloodline for free without even drinking their blood, because your blood descends from theirs. Once again, the fluff implies that this isn't usually a choice, but something that happens on its own. It's only a choice for the player, not the character.<br /> <br /> Some 1e bloodlines worked for multiple clans, but in general the rule I think is that it's tied to a clan because it's a mutation of that clan. Once again, not a faction but a fundamental quality of a given vampire's blood, much like their Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:31:32-07:00","id":557121,"title":"","content":"Thanks =D<br /> <br /> Okay, so what prevents anyone else from joining? What would happen if a Daeva from drinking the blood of a Brujah in hopes to join their ranks? I can see issues with Disciplines. No matter what, deep down they aren't 'pure' Brujah, not being from their parent Clan. My work around would simply be the Discipline that makes them what they are (in this case I think it would be Vigor (at least in 1E)), is transferred to the new member, becoming an in-clan Discipline. If it is solely because they have to be from that parent clan, I will accept that. It just somewhat boggles my brain.<br /> <br /> =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:33:49-07:00","id":557125,"title":"","content":"Thanks Maina (you responded while I was still typing lol)<br /> <br /> Okay okay, so that makes a bit more sense. However, what would stop one from trying? (Thinking some sort of ritualistic style resembling Dragon Age: Origins and becoming a Warden. It 'taints' their blood, making them something else)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:38:40-07:00","id":557135,"title":"","content":"Not everyone is focused and fervent or unique enough to really manage it. I think the 'youngest' bloodline is the Sons of Cade, from one of the Night Horrors books. I don't think he's even embraced anyone, but he's just changed enough that he's capable of spreading his bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:49:34-07:00","id":557154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines?p=557125#post557125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Maina (you responded while I was still typing lol)<br /> <br /> Okay okay, so that makes a bit more sense. However, what would stop one from trying? (Thinking some sort of ritualistic style resembling Dragon Age: Origins and becoming a Warden. It 'taints' their blood, making them something else)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To use a somewhat flimsy analogy, the Clans are like separate species and Bloodlines are like subspecies. You can't join a Bloodline that has a different parent Clan because your blood is just too different from theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-16-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T11:53:58-07:00","id":557176,"title":"","content":"Thanks Charlaquin!<br /> <br /> Okay, I shall accept that. That terminology seems to put things into place. Thanks =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:31:01-07:00","id":557267,"title":"","content":"You could have an almost identical bloodline for a different clan though. They would likely be unrelated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:48:59-07:00","id":557300,"title":"","content":"Char said the best. There were a few rare bloodlines in 1st edition that seemed have affinity for two clans but there isn't much info on how that happened.<br /> They may not be a thing now in 2nd.<br /> Another thing to keep in mind that Requiem clans are not unlike the old lineages in Masquerade with Requiem Bloodlines more akin to Masquerade Clans.<br /> <br /> One more thing look at Malkavia, the affliction in Lords of the Damned( another Malk port).<br /> 1st edition Ventrue picked derangements easier than the others hence the Malkovians and Malkavia treatment.<br /> It is problematic in the 2nd edition since derangements were done away with. But could be done with conditions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:30:44-07:00","id":558159,"title":"","content":"Diggs, good point. Technicalities!<br /> <br /> Chattnos. I never really put those two together. I can see why they made it a Bloodline then. Although I think it would still be fantastic if anyone drinks from a Malkavian they are at risk of developing the madness. Like a vampire STD. =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T06:54:57-07:00","id":558202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines#post557071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;DR why are Bloodlines restricted to certain clans. Ex. Gangrel -&gt; Brujah?Thanks =D</div> </div> </div> </div> Because bloodlines are literally what they say on the can. They're a lineage of vampires who've developed special abilities. Its passed down from sire to childer. Sometimes, you have a skip, or the like, but its an inherited trait from your vampire familial line.<br /> <br /> Now, you can also &quot;adopt&quot; yourself into another family. That's what Avus are for. You're leaving your original family and forging (blood?) ties with a new family. <br /> <br /> This has nothing to do with philosphy, it has everything to do with whom you were Embraced as. Vampire genes, if you will. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T07:13:52-07:00","id":558221,"title":"","content":"MCN thanks =D<br /> <br /> Ya, that's what Charlaquin was saying (I think). I also can completely get behind that. It is because it is.<br /> <br /> Side note: I like the idea of a house rule that let's you perform a ritual to join one. It would be both physically/mentally taxing. Requiring a decent amount of blood (not just that from the bloodline member). You are also at risk of developing multiple derangements/conditions. The least being 'Addiction'. Also at risk of burning down a lot of bridges. Your sire, maybe even your clan, might 'disown' you. See you as a traitor. You'd be an abomination in their eyes. Saying all of this, what's the benefit? =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T07:51:47-07:00","id":558233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines?p=558221#post558221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note: I like the idea of a house rule that let's you perform a ritual to join one. It would be both physically/mentally taxing. Requiring a decent amount of blood (not just that from the bloodline member). You are also at risk of developing multiple derangements/conditions. The least being 'Addiction'. Also at risk of burning down a lot of bridges. Your sire, maybe even your clan, might 'disown' you. See you as a traitor. You'd be an abomination in their eyes. Saying all of this, what's the benefit? =D</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't even really need a house rule for that. Most vampires aren't aware of the exact mechanics for joining a bloodline, so a ritualized method to justify the blood drinking and effort of will to make the turn are actually fairly common. <br /> <br /> The vampires generally don't know the underlying mechanics or reason why the ritual works, all they know is that it generally does work. Short of an Ordo Dracul experiment, most won't see the point in varying from the ritual, and quite possibly think that the ritual itself is the only way. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:05:03-07:00","id":558264,"title":"","content":"MCN - Good point. Who's to say that it isn't what normally happens?<br /> <br /> Thanks =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:53:38-07:00","id":558313,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure where I stand on Outsiders joining a bloodline. Especially since it assumed in 2.0 that most of a given clan are blood related getwise.<br /> <br /> Most of the cross clan Bloodlines had theme and involved just two clans And the Bloodline involved them becoming closer to each other in disciplines and banes.<br /> like a nos mekhet line were the Nos got Auspex and the mekhet got nightmare. Gangrel ventrue would be even easier.<br /> Then again such a bloodline could just be two bloodlines that mimic each other.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:34:41-07:00","id":558405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines?p=558159#post558159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chattnos. I never really put those two together. I can see why they made it a Bloodline then. Although I think it would still be fantastic if anyone drinks from a Malkavian they are at risk of developing the madness. Like a vampire STD. =D</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how Malkavia the disease worked in the Ventrue Clan book. It was not technically a Bloodline, but worked similarly to one in that it gave you an additional Discipline (Dementation) and an additional weakness (a Derrangement), but it could affect vampires of any Clan. There was a sidebar about running it as a universal Bloodline as well. If you're running 1e it works as written. If you're running 2e, I did a conversion of it you can use, it's in the homebrew hub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:46:49-07:00","id":558417,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin - I shall have to look! I am intrigued now. Homebrew hooeeee!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:28:12-07:00","id":558829,"title":"","content":"IIRC there was a 1ed bloodline that was a mix of Nosferatu and Gangrel. If two clans have two shared disciplines then it is simple to just make the fourth the other clan's third. I don't remember exactly if a member of one clan could bring a member of another clan, but technically, it was Bloodline X has two branches, one for Clan A and one for Clan B. The branches were identical except in that their members started in different clans. You can still do that in 2ed then add additional bloodline stuff on top of that. I think you only are restricted by forcing Clan A to be in the Clan A branch and brought into the bloodline by a Clan A branch member. Ritually, you would likely require an avus from each clan anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:40:35-07:00","id":558838,"title":"","content":"1e had a hand full of Bloodlines that multiple Clans could join. It's World of Darkness, the only rule without exceptions is that there are exceptions to every (other) rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:53:54-07:00","id":558858,"title":"","content":"Gotta love Eddie Vines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:57:57-07:00","id":560372,"title":"","content":"Blood and Smoke refers to elder vampires having a sense that they are on the cusp of metamorphosing into something more than one they are, something new and terrible. I get the impression that founding a bloodline is part of this process, though perhaps only the first step...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-19-2015, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:41:42-07:00","id":560751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines?p=560372#post560372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood and Smoke refers to elder vampires having a sense that they are on the cusp of metamorphosing into something more than one they are, something new and terrible. I get the impression that founding a bloodline is part of this process, though perhaps only the first step...</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that's a reference to becoming a Methuselah, not opening a new bloodline. Golconda's kinda faded into the background in favor of becoming an unstoppable creature like the Unholy or the Blind Mother.<br /> <br /> It seems to be a thing with most gamelines now, becoming something high level. Methuselah, Archmage, Gentry, reaching Hell, achieving Apothesis, Beast's Inheritance. Prometheans reach the New Dawn, and Sin-Eaters can lay their Geist to rest and let them move on, both supers becoming human again. Hunter (for obvious reasons) and Werewolf (might have missed it?) are the only games that don't seem to have a high tier evolution, imho. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:11:16-07:00","id":560785,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well now granted, so was my initial character. He was a power hungry Malkav who Diablerized and didn't afraid of anything. Well, he made it so that his aura made him look human actually, also, not insane! No one knew what he was! Just that he was.. Wrong. Didn't help that he was had a split personality which one was a manic depressant and the other a psychopath (was kind of hard playing no emotions at times). Eat ALL the enemies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:41:07-07:00","id":560811,"title":"","content":"Quick aside. Manic depressive is an outdated term, it's actually called Bipolar disorder now. Similarly, psychopathy is also outdated; it is now refered to as antisocial personality disorder, and people who suffer from it do have a normal emotional range, they just don't experience empathy. Unfortunately, one of the problems with Malkavians is that it's very difficult to portray severe mental illness accurately, especially when there are still a lot of widely held misconceptions about mental and social disorders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:59:33-07:00","id":560838,"title":"","content":"Yar, I'm not a fan of the term Bipolar. Sure it's easier to say (and kind of makes more sense), but Manic Depressive just sounds more suitable for a gothic style game. Same with Psychopath. Ya, it's almost a taboo now. Anyone who is labelled with that is almost instantly ostracized in society. But still, a more fitting term. Also yes, they do feel emotions and not empathy; however, they also tend to not show much in the ways of emotions. Sociopaths do, and they can even get along with like-minded individuals. But not so much for the latter (unless it suits their needs, which being a vampire who was in torpor for an incredibly long time, he didn't want to be around anyone/trust anyone. So he showed no emotions, or if any, disdain to most individuals).<br /> <br /> Also I completely agree. Mental/social disorders are not taking as seriously as they should be. I am glad to finally see some physician's taking it seriously now. But we are a long way off from what we should be. It is also difficult to play them out as well, especially if you aren't trying to offend anyone (which is rather hard to do these days). Which is why I went for those two. Either incredibly happy/sad/angry, or no emotion. Randomly roll a d10. 1-5 = Manic. 6-10 = Psycho. If manic, 1-3 = angry, 4-6 = sad, 7-10 = happy (yes, there was one extra for happy, but it was easier to play!) It was incredibly fun to play. Added extra depth. Mood swings like a muffin though. Especially if angry. So many frenzy checks 0.o<br /> <br /> Also, this is all from my understanding of the illnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T10:58:05-07:00","id":560939,"title":"","content":"I think modeling the behavior of Malkavians on real world mental illnesses is both offensive and asking for a flanderization. <br /> <br /> When people ask you not to refer to something like that by an outdated named Krzyzstof, it's generally because it's considered offensive. That's also not actually how Bipolar works in terms of the mood swings, it's a media misconception that they're so sudden that you cycle between extremely happy/sad/angry rapidly.<br /> <br /> My twin brother is Bipolar, and seeing this sort of casual misrepresentation is exactly the sort of thing that can really put me in a bad mood. It's a free world, and I can't make you stop, but I urge you to consider if what you were/are portraying is accurate and whether it's in poor taste or not.<br /> <br /> This is a general problem with Malkavians and also with the 1e Ventrue weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:08:29-07:00","id":561193,"title":"","content":"Well it was not my intention to offend. We were making characters in group, I wanted to play an insane character. Chose Multiple Personality and joked around with everyone about what each one would be. Essentially, Very Eccentric in every way with Huge mood swings and the other having next to no emotions or at least not portraying any. So we were talking about what illnesses do those best fall into and boom, we got those. Not that Bipolar is strictly labelled as such, it's actually one of the more complicated ones out there (I have a couple friends with it so I know how touchy it can be as well, and yes, it is a huge piss off when people don't take it seriously) Also, I don't think anyone actually said to not refer to those with outdated terms. Just simply stating that they are outdated terms.<br /> <br /> I do understand that it can be a touchy subject. It is everywhere. Even to those who suffer from, well, any mental illness too. No one ever seems to take them seriously (as i mentioned before).<br /> <br /> But like I said, I don't mean to offend, it's just usually easier to describe them as such since most people understand what they mean, or at least know of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T16:30:09-07:00","id":561319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines?p=560751#post560751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that's a reference to becoming a Methuselah, not opening a new bloodline. Golconda's kinda faded into the background in favor of becoming an unstoppable creature like the Unholy or the Blind Mother.<br /> <br /> It seems to be a thing with most gamelines now, becoming something high level. Methuselah, Archmage, Gentry, reaching Hell, achieving Apothesis, Beast's Inheritance. Prometheans reach the New Dawn, and Sin-Eaters can lay their Geist to rest and let them move on, both supers becoming human again. Hunter (for obvious reasons) and Werewolf (might have missed it?) are the only games that don't seem to have a high tier evolution, imho.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're probably right, though I kind of feel like I don't get how Methuselahs became such a &quot;thing&quot; in VtR. Have they been mentioned anywhere outside the writeup for Zagreus in Immortal Sinners? There, the title specifically refers to his perfect memory, which is somewhat less of a big deal now that the Fog of Eternity is no longer a thing. It's still remarkable, sure, and almost certainly some kind of supernatural ability, but he seems like mostly just a really old vampire with some crazy-powerful really old vampire Devotions.<br /> <br /> In any event, the fact remains that founding a Bloodline explicitly (as per Blood and Smoke) requires a vampire to have a Blood Potency of 6, and that it's a profound, irreversible change that allows a vampire to do things that vampires otherwise can't do. It's about the closest thing to evolving into something new that elder vampires are known to be able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-19-2015, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T16:11:01-07:00","id":562309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines?p=561319#post561319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In any event, the fact remains that founding a Bloodline explicitly (as per Blood and Smoke) requires a vampire to have a Blood Potency of 6, and that it's a profound, irreversible change that allows a vampire to do things that vampires otherwise can't do. It's about the closest thing to evolving into something new that elder vampires are known to be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so then question. Can you create an additional bloodline? So for example, way back when before Brujah were a thing. A Gangrel 'evolves' into a Brujah, creating that bloodline. Would it then be possible for that same vampire to create an additional one? Something beyond Brujah? Or, can someone in a bloodline, say a different Brujah, create a different bloodline from that? <br /> <br /> I guess what I am asking is; What are the limits to creating bloodlines?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T17:51:18-07:00","id":562388,"title":"","content":"You can only be a member of a single bloodline, so no, you can't found more than one, and a member of a bloodline cannot found <i>another</i> bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:55:38-07:00","id":562594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/557071-bloodlines?p=561193#post561193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it was not my intention to offend. We were making characters in group, I wanted to play an insane character. Chose Multiple Personality and joked around with everyone about what each one would be. Essentially, Very Eccentric in every way with Huge mood swings and the other having next to no emotions or at least not portraying any. So we were talking about what illnesses do those best fall into and boom, we got those. Not that Bipolar is strictly labelled as such, it's actually one of the more complicated ones out there (I have a couple friends with it so I know how touchy it can be as well, and yes, it is a huge piss off when people don't take it seriously) Also, I don't think anyone actually said to not refer to those with outdated terms. Just simply stating that they are outdated terms.<br /> <br /> I do understand that it can be a touchy subject. It is everywhere. Even to those who suffer from, well, any mental illness too. No one ever seems to take them seriously (as i mentioned before).<br /> <br /> But like I said, I don't mean to offend, it's just usually easier to describe them as such since most people understand what they mean, or at least know of them</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you are trying for. The problem is even the professionals don't agree on the terms or if some conditions even exist.<br /> The existence of multiple personalities is one. Is Asperger's part of the autism spectrum is another.<br /> If you go down that road do a lot of research and stick to more common conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}